Here is the semantic interpretation of the scene based on the provided ontology:

---

### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "HeavyRainLaneChangeScenario" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :vehicle1, :vehicle2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 ;
    :hasObstacle :roadCondition1 .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Lead vehicle in left lane" .

:vehicle2 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Following vehicle in right lane attempting lane change" .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition ;
    :description "Heavy rain reducing visibility and traction" .

:risk1 a :RearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :description "High risk of rear-end collision due to reduced visibility and braking distance" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of lane intrusion during lane change in poor weather conditions" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Slippery road conditions increasing skid and hydroplaning risk" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:roadCondition1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Wet road surface with standing water" .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.8"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .
```

